window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-resources/b458-eebece740824507a.json"]={sha256:"eebece740824507a001dd3e609a1079d90e2dd6788b4d7e2d93fe8de5bb84099",value:{"sources":[{"id":"b-src-environment","title":"Research on Innovative and Alternative Wastewater Technologies","url":"https://www.epa.gov/sustainable-water-infrastructure/research-innovative-and-alternative-wastewater-technologies","publisher":"U.S. Environmental Protection Agency","scope":"Category overview: wastewater technologies and treatment references. Not individual verification of every named environmental project."},{"id":"b-src-waste","title":"Sustainable Materials Management","url":"https://www.epa.gov/smm","publisher":"U.S. Environmental Protection Agency","scope":"Category overview: materials life cycles, waste prevention, recycling and recovery."},{"id":"b-src-wastewater","title":"Wastewater Technology Fact Sheets","url":"https://www.epa.gov/septic/wastewater-technology-fact-sheets","publisher":"U.S. Environmental Protection Agency","scope":"Category overview: disinfection, constructed wetlands, package plants, sewer technologies and treatment."},{"id":"v17s-urban-green","title":"綠色基礎設施類型","titleEn":"Types of Green Infrastructure","url":"https://www.epa.gov/green-infrastructure/types-green-infrastructure","organization":"US EPA","accessed":"2026-10-23","publisher":"US EPA","scope":"來源支持原理或工程背景；算例為明示教學假設。","scopeEn":"Source supports principles or project context; examples use explicit teaching assumptions."},{"id":"v17s-urban-swmm","title":"暴雨逕流與低衝擊開發模型","titleEn":"Storm Water Management Model (SWMM)","url":"https://www.epa.gov/water-research/storm-water-management-model-swmm","organization":"US EPA","accessed":"2026-10-23","publisher":"US EPA","scope":"來源支持原理或工程背景；算例為明示教學假設。","scopeEn":"Source supports principles or project context; examples use explicit teaching assumptions."}],"media":{"courses":[{"courseId":"b458","videos":[],"guides":[{"id":"b458-v17-practice","title":"工程操作與定量驗證手冊","titleEn":"Engineering actions and quantitative verification","concept":"以「孔隙堵塞、清掃復原與承載排水協調」為主線，依序完成十個專題單元。學徒在場景中辨識設備、列出邊界、重算明示的教學算例、比較量測與模型，最後診斷故障並交付證據。每一單元保留機制、算例、驗證與失效四種學習任務。","conceptEn":"Follow pore clogging, cleaning recovery and structural drainage through ten technical units. Identify equipment in the scene, define boundaries, reproduce explicitly hypothetical examples, compare measurements with models, and diagnose faults before handing over evidence. Each unit contains mechanism, calculation, verification and failure tasks.","procedure":["在「有效透水面積」的教學模型或試算表中先重現 460 m2，再依驗證任務改動一個輸入、保留其餘條件。對照「把不透水補丁仍算透水面會高估排水。」的異常情境，提交基準與變更後數值、單位及一項能區分兩者的量測。","在「現場入滲測試」的教學模型或試算表中先重現 1 m/h，再依驗證任務改動一個輸入、保留其餘條件。對照「只挑最乾淨位置會掩蓋高負荷區堵塞。」的異常情境，提交基準與變更後數值、單位及一項能區分兩者的量測。","在「儲水底層容量」的教學模型或試算表中先重現 37.5 m3，再依驗證任務改動一個輸入、保留其餘條件。對照「地下水已淹入底層時仍報全部容量會重複計算。」的異常情境，提交基準與變更後數值、單位及一項能區分兩者的量測。","在「細粒輸入與孔喉」的教學模型或試算表中先重現 100 kg/year，再依驗證任務改動一個輸入、保留其餘條件。對照「泥沙由鄰地持續流入會讓清掃效果短暫。」的異常情境，提交基準與變更後數值、單位及一項能區分兩者的量測。","在「串聯水力阻力」的教學模型或試算表中先重現 10 relative resistance，再依驗證任務改動一個輸入、保留其餘條件。對照「忽略最慢土基會把表面恢復誤認全系統恢復。」的異常情境，提交基準與變更後數值、單位及一項能區分兩者的量測。","在「真空清掃復原率」的教學模型或試算表中先重現 0.75 fraction，再依驗證任務改動一個輸入、保留其餘條件。對照「外觀乾淨但深層細粒仍在，入滲未必全復原。」的異常情境，提交基準與變更後數值、單位及一項能區分兩者的量測。","在「含水與承載」的教學模型或試算表中先重現 500 kPa，再依驗證任務改動一個輸入、保留其餘條件。對照「只追求高孔隙而不驗結構會增加車轍風險。」的異常情境，提交基準與變更後數值、單位及一項能區分兩者的量測。","在「底排失效辨識」的教學模型或試算表中先重現 0.1 m，再依驗證任務改動一個輸入、保留其餘條件。對照「只看到無出流就判定土壤吸收全部水量可能錯誤。」的異常情境，提交基準與變更後數值、單位及一項能區分兩者的量測。","在「污染滯留與去向」的教學模型或試算表中先重現 9 g/event，再依驗證任務改動一個輸入、保留其餘條件。對照「把滯留當分解會遺失污染存量管理。」的異常情境，提交基準與變更後數值、單位及一項能區分兩者的量測。","在「分區維護優先序」的教學模型或試算表中先重現 12 ordinal score，再依驗證任務改動一個輸入、保留其餘條件。對照「只依面積大者優先可能漏掉關鍵出入口。」的異常情境，提交基準與變更後數值、單位及一項能區分兩者的量測。"],"procedureEn":["In the teaching model or spreadsheet for effective permeable area, first reproduce 460 m2, then vary one input following the verification task while holding other conditions fixed. Contrast the fault scenario \"Counting impermeable patches overstates drainage.\" and submit baseline and changed values, units, and one measurement that distinguishes them.","In the teaching model or spreadsheet for field infiltration testing, first reproduce 1 m/h, then vary one input following the verification task while holding other conditions fixed. Contrast the fault scenario \"Testing the cleanest spot hides loaded-area clogging.\" and submit baseline and changed values, units, and one measurement that distinguishes them.","In the teaching model or spreadsheet for base storage capacity, first reproduce 37.5 m3, then vary one input following the verification task while holding other conditions fixed. Contrast the fault scenario \"Reporting full capacity in a flooded base double counts occupied storage.\" and submit baseline and changed values, units, and one measurement that distinguishes them.","In the teaching model or spreadsheet for fine-particle loading and pore throats, first reproduce 100 kg/year, then vary one input following the verification task while holding other conditions fixed. Contrast the fault scenario \"Continuing sediment inflow makes cleaning gains temporary.\" and submit baseline and changed values, units, and one measurement that distinguishes them.","In the teaching model or spreadsheet for hydraulic resistance in series, first reproduce 10 relative resistance, then vary one input following the verification task while holding other conditions fixed. Contrast the fault scenario \"Ignoring the slow subgrade confuses surface recovery with system recovery.\" and submit baseline and changed values, units, and one measurement that distinguishes them.","In the teaching model or spreadsheet for vacuum-cleaning recovery, first reproduce 0.75 fraction, then vary one input following the verification task while holding other conditions fixed. Contrast the fault scenario \"A clean appearance can leave deeply trapped fines.\" and submit baseline and changed values, units, and one measurement that distinguishes them.","In the teaching model or spreadsheet for moisture and bearing performance, first reproduce 500 kPa, then vary one input following the verification task while holding other conditions fixed. Contrast the fault scenario \"Pursuing porosity without structural checks increases rutting risk.\" and submit baseline and changed values, units, and one measurement that distinguishes them.","In the teaching model or spreadsheet for underdrain fault diagnosis, first reproduce 0.1 m, then vary one input following the verification task while holding other conditions fixed. Contrast the fault scenario \"No discharge does not prove all water infiltrated into soil.\" and submit baseline and changed values, units, and one measurement that distinguishes them.","In the teaching model or spreadsheet for pollutant retention and fate, first reproduce 9 g/event, then vary one input following the verification task while holding other conditions fixed. Contrast the fault scenario \"Treating retention as destruction loses inventory control.\" and submit baseline and changed values, units, and one measurement that distinguishes them.","In the teaching model or spreadsheet for prioritize maintenance zones, first reproduce 12 ordinal score, then vary one input following the verification task while holding other conditions fixed. Contrast the fault scenario \"Area-only priority can miss critical entrances.\" and submit baseline and changed values, units, and one measurement that distinguishes them."],"evidence":["標出停車格補丁並更新有效面積。","在車輪帶與非車輪帶分別重複測試。","提高地下水位使可用厚度減半。","比較入口邊緣與中間區的粒徑分布。","將表層阻力減半並比較總阻力變化。","比較清掃前0.2、後0.6和初始0.8的差異。","比較乾濕情境下的教學撓度資料。","同時量測上游水位與出口尾水。","比較截留量與清掃收集量，追蹤未回收部分。","對三個分區排序並說明資料不足處。"],"evidenceEn":["Map parking-space patches and update effective area.","Repeat tests in wheel tracks and non-wheel areas.","Raise groundwater so available thickness halves.","Compare particle-size distributions at edges and the centre.","Halve surface resistance and compare total resistance.","Compare pre-clean0.2, post-clean0.6 and initial0.8.","Compare teaching deflection data in dry and wet cases.","Measure upstream and tailwater levels simultaneously.","Compare retention with collected cleaning residue and track the remainder.","Rank three zones and note data gaps."],"pitfalls":["把不透水補丁仍算透水面會高估排水。","只挑最乾淨位置會掩蓋高負荷區堵塞。","地下水已淹入底層時仍報全部容量會重複計算。","泥沙由鄰地持續流入會讓清掃效果短暫。","忽略最慢土基會把表面恢復誤認全系統恢復。","外觀乾淨但深層細粒仍在，入滲未必全復原。","只追求高孔隙而不驗結構會增加車轍風險。","只看到無出流就判定土壤吸收全部水量可能錯誤。","把滯留當分解會遺失污染存量管理。","只依面積大者優先可能漏掉關鍵出入口。"],"pitfallsEn":["Counting impermeable patches overstates drainage.","Testing the cleanest spot hides loaded-area clogging.","Reporting full capacity in a flooded base double counts occupied storage.","Continuing sediment inflow makes cleaning gains temporary.","Ignoring the slow subgrade confuses surface recovery with system recovery.","A clean appearance can leave deeply trapped fines.","Pursuing porosity without structural checks increases rutting risk.","No discharge does not prove all water infiltrated into soil.","Treating retention as destruction loses inventory control.","Area-only priority can miss critical entrances."],"sourceIds":["v17s-urban-green","v17s-urban-swmm"],"sources":[{"id":"v17s-urban-green","title":"綠色基礎設施類型","titleEn":"Types of Green Infrastructure","url":"https://www.epa.gov/green-infrastructure/types-green-infrastructure","organization":"US EPA","accessed":"2026-10-23","publisher":"US EPA","scope":"來源支持原理或工程背景；算例為明示教學假設。","scopeEn":"Source supports principles or project context; examples use explicit teaching assumptions."},{"id":"v17s-urban-swmm","title":"暴雨逕流與低衝擊開發模型","titleEn":"Storm Water Management Model (SWMM)","url":"https://www.epa.gov/water-research/storm-water-management-model-swmm","organization":"US EPA","accessed":"2026-10-23","publisher":"US EPA","scope":"來源支持原理或工程背景；算例為明示教學假設。","scopeEn":"Source supports principles or project context; examples use explicit teaching assumptions."}],"simulationOnly":true,"scope":"公開原理與資料支持的原創教學。算例中的輸入為明示教學假設，非該設施實測或操作設定。此處任務在離線模型完成，不能作為現場設計、飲用水合格或設備操作許可。","scopeEn":"Original teaching based on public principles and sources. Numerical inputs are explicit teaching assumptions, not site measurements or operating setpoints. Tasks use offline models and do not certify field design, potable-water compliance or equipment operation."}]}]},"related":{"courses":[{"courseId":"b458","overview":"跨單元連結與比較練習","overviewEn":"Cross-process connections and comparisons","related":[{"id":"b415","title":"首爾清溪川復育","titleEn":"Seoul Cheonggyecheon restoration","why":"比較兩個系統的物質或能量收支，列出不可直接沿用的邊界條件。","whyEn":"Compare material or energy balances and identify boundary conditions that cannot be transferred.","transfer":"守恆、量測與失效驗證","transferEn":"Conservation, measurement and failure verification","difference":"設備尺度、進料組成與品質目標必須分別設定。","differenceEn":"Equipment scale, feed composition and quality objectives require separate definitions.","practice":["各選一個教學算例，記下輸入、輸出與單位。","對照兩課的系統邊界，說明哪些假設不能沿用。","改變一個輸入，提出量測與失效判據來核對結果。"],"practiceEn":["Choose one worked example from each course and record inputs, outputs and units.","Compare system boundaries and identify assumptions that cannot transfer.","Change one input and propose measurements and failure criteria to check the result."],"place":{"name":"首爾代表點","nameEn":"Seoul reference point","country":"南韓","countryEn":"South Korea","lat":37.57,"lon":126.98,"coordinateScope":"approximate-city-reference; not a facility entrance","lng":126.98,"coordinateScopeEn":"Approximate public facility/research reference, not an operating entrance or the teaching laboratory."},"referenceUrls":["https://www.epa.gov/sustainable-water-infrastructure/research-innovative-and-alternative-wastewater-technologies","https://www.epa.gov/smm","https://www.epa.gov/septic/wastewater-technology-fact-sheets"]},{"id":"b416","title":"新加坡碧山—宏茂橋公園河川復育","titleEn":"Bishan–Ang Mo Kio Park river restoration","why":"比較兩個系統的物質或能量收支，列出不可直接沿用的邊界條件。","whyEn":"Compare material or energy balances and identify boundary conditions that cannot be transferred.","transfer":"守恆、量測與失效驗證","transferEn":"Conservation, measurement and failure verification","difference":"設備尺度、進料組成與品質目標必須分別設定。","differenceEn":"Equipment scale, feed composition and quality objectives require separate definitions.","practice":["各選一個教學算例，記下輸入、輸出與單位。","對照兩課的系統邊界，說明哪些假設不能沿用。","改變一個輸入，提出量測與失效判據來核對結果。"],"practiceEn":["Choose one worked example from each course and record inputs, outputs and units.","Compare system boundaries and identify assumptions that cannot transfer.","Change one input and propose measurements and failure criteria to check the result."],"place":{"name":"新加坡","nameEn":"Singapore","country":"新加坡","countryEn":"Singapore","lat":1.35,"lon":103.82,"coordinateScope":"approximate-city-reference; not a facility entrance","lng":103.82,"coordinateScopeEn":"Approximate public facility/research reference, not an operating entrance or the teaching laboratory."},"referenceUrls":["https://www.epa.gov/sustainable-water-infrastructure/research-innovative-and-alternative-wastewater-technologies","https://www.epa.gov/smm","https://www.epa.gov/septic/wastewater-technology-fact-sheets"]}],"references":[{"id":"b-src-environment","title":"Research on Innovative and Alternative Wastewater Technologies","url":"https://www.epa.gov/sustainable-water-infrastructure/research-innovative-and-alternative-wastewater-technologies","publisher":"U.S. Environmental Protection Agency","scope":"Category overview: wastewater technologies and treatment references. Not individual verification of every named environmental project."},{"id":"b-src-waste","title":"Sustainable Materials Management","url":"https://www.epa.gov/smm","publisher":"U.S. Environmental Protection Agency","scope":"Category overview: materials life cycles, waste prevention, recycling and recovery."},{"id":"b-src-wastewater","title":"Wastewater Technology Fact Sheets","url":"https://www.epa.gov/septic/wastewater-technology-fact-sheets","publisher":"U.S. Environmental Protection Agency","scope":"Category overview: disinfection, constructed wetlands, package plants, sewer technologies and treatment."},{"id":"v17s-urban-green","title":"綠色基礎設施類型","titleEn":"Types of Green Infrastructure","url":"https://www.epa.gov/green-infrastructure/types-green-infrastructure","organization":"US EPA","accessed":"2026-10-23","publisher":"US EPA","scope":"來源支持原理或工程背景；算例為明示教學假設。","scopeEn":"Source supports principles or project context; examples use explicit teaching assumptions."},{"id":"v17s-urban-swmm","title":"暴雨逕流與低衝擊開發模型","titleEn":"Storm Water Management Model (SWMM)","url":"https://www.epa.gov/water-research/storm-water-management-model-swmm","organization":"US EPA","accessed":"2026-10-23","publisher":"US EPA","scope":"來源支持原理或工程背景；算例為明示教學假設。","scopeEn":"Source supports principles or project context; examples use explicit teaching assumptions."}]}]},"places":{"courses":[{"courseId":"b458","place":{"name":"美國EPA總部：方法資料來源機構（非實廠）","nameEn":"US EPA headquarters: methodology source institution (not a process plant)","country":"美國","countryEn":"United States","lat":38.8941,"lon":-77.0298,"coordinateScope":"近似機構所在區域位置；依公開地址作教材地圖代表點，非建物入口、實廠、實測或導航位置。","coordinateScopeEn":"Approximate institution-area location inferred from its public address for the teaching map; not a building entrance, process plant, surveyed point or navigation coordinate.","locationSourceUrl":"https://www.epa.gov/aboutepa/visiting-epa-headquarters","locationVerified":"2026-10-23","lng":-77.0298},"summary":"本課以來源所列的技術指引與研究為閱讀脈絡，並非重建某一設施的工程沿革；算例、數據與場景參數皆為原創教學假設。比較舊方法與感測、控制、資源回收整合的方法時，先固定處理功能及系統邊界，再評估效率與可靠度。","summaryEn":"The cited technical guidance and research provide a reading pathway, not the engineering history of a particular facility. Examples, data and scene parameters are original teaching assumptions. When comparing conventional methods with integrated sensing, control and resource recovery, hold the treatment function and system boundary fixed before assessing efficiency and reliability.","history":[{"year":"工程背景","title":"透水鋪面孔隙維護","titleEn":"Pervious-pavement pore maintenance","text":"本課以來源所列的技術指引與研究為閱讀脈絡，並非重建某一設施的工程沿革；算例、數據與場景參數皆為原創教學假設。比較舊方法與感測、控制、資源回收整合的方法時，先固定處理功能及系統邊界，再評估效率與可靠度。","textEn":"The cited technical guidance and research provide a reading pathway, not the engineering history of a particular facility. Examples, data and scene parameters are original teaching assumptions. When comparing conventional methods with integrated sensing, control and resource recovery, hold the treatment function and system boundary fixed before assessing efficiency and reliability."}],"connection":"以「孔隙堵塞、清掃復原與承載排水協調」為主線，依序完成十個專題單元。學徒在場景中辨識設備、列出邊界、重算明示的教學算例、比較量測與模型，最後診斷故障並交付證據。每一單元保留機制、算例、驗證與失效四種學習任務。","connectionEn":"Follow pore clogging, cleaning recovery and structural drainage through ten technical units. Identify equipment in the scene, define boundaries, reproduce explicitly hypothetical examples, compare measurements with models, and diagnose faults before handing over evidence. Each unit contains mechanism, calculation, verification and failure tasks.","references":[{"id":"v17s-urban-green","title":"綠色基礎設施類型","titleEn":"Types of Green Infrastructure","url":"https://www.epa.gov/green-infrastructure/types-green-infrastructure","organization":"US EPA","accessed":"2026-10-23","publisher":"US EPA","scope":"來源支持原理或工程背景；算例為明示教學假設。","scopeEn":"Source supports principles or project context; examples use explicit teaching assumptions."},{"id":"v17s-urban-swmm","title":"暴雨逕流與低衝擊開發模型","titleEn":"Storm Water Management Model (SWMM)","url":"https://www.epa.gov/water-research/storm-water-management-model-swmm","organization":"US EPA","accessed":"2026-10-23","publisher":"US EPA","scope":"來源支持原理或工程背景；算例為明示教學假設。","scopeEn":"Source supports principles or project context; examples use explicit teaching assumptions."}],"sourceIds":["v17s-urban-green","v17s-urban-swmm"]}]},"vendors":{"courses":[],"vendors":[]}}};
